.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 

.SS "template<class T>
.br
template<class U = T, bool Verified = true>
.br
class cbor::schema< T >::accessor< U, Verified >"Reads the part \fRU\fP of a message of \fRT\fP\&. 

A path that starts with \fR@\fP starts at \fRU\fP\&. A path that starts with \fR$\fP starts at the root\&. The result is a \fRstd::expected\fP: the value of a number, \fRbool\fP or enum; a \fRstd::string_view\fP of a text; the accessor of a struct, a list or a map\&. Every result holds the owner of the bytes\&. The accessor of a \fRstd::variant<A\&.\&.\&.>\fP member has \fRindex()\fP and \fRget<A>()\fP\&. \fRindex()\fP gives the index of the alternative that the head of its item names\&. \fRget<A>()\fP gives a class alternative as its accessor, a number, \fRbool\fP or enum as its value, and a text or byte string as a \fRstd::string_view\fP into the message\&. Another alternative gives \fRincorrect_type\fP\&. A path ends at a variant member: \fR$\&.pet\&.name\fP does not compile\&. \fRview\fP gives a \fBcbor::typed_array_view\fP of a list of numbers\&. It exists on the root accessor only\&. \fRsize()\fP gives the count of a list or a map\&. An accessor of a vector of fixed-size structs is a random access range of \fRfixed_element\fP accessors\&. \fR\fBat_path\fP\fP on a temporary does not compile\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
accessor\&.at_path<"@\&.member">(indexes\&.\&.\&.) → std::expected<V, cbor::error>
accessor\&.at_path<"$\&.member">(indexes\&.\&.\&.) → std::expected<V, cbor::error>
root\&.view<"$\&.list">(indexes\&.\&.\&.)          → std::expected<cbor::typed_array_view<E>, cbor::error>
accessor\&.size()                          → std::size_t
pet\&.index()                              → std::size_t
pet\&.get<A>()                             → std::expected<accessor<A>, cbor::error>
accessor\&.begin()                         → iterator
accessor\&.end()                           → iterator
.fi
.PP
 
